; ============================================================================
; com.1retro.forge - what a Forge parser read out of a save, and which parser
;
; One key rather than two, because the halves are useless apart: a bag of
; parsed values says nothing without the name of the parser that produced it,
; and that name alone says only that something ran.
;
; Non-normative. The Forge specification will live in this repository and will
; define this properly; until then the envelope carries the two things that are
; known, and this file records that shape so the page and its example cannot
; drift. Written closed for that reason: a bundle carrying a shape Forge added
; later stays valid either way, since to the saves format an extension value is
; `any`.
;
; The root here is the value carried under the key, not a bundle.
; ============================================================================

forge = {
  0 => tstr,          ; which parser read the save ("alttp", "ff7")
  ? 1 => parsed,      ; what it found
}

; Deliberately unconstrained. What this holds depends on the game and on the
; parser version, so keys and values are Forge's: integer, text, or anything
; else CBOR carries. A consumer that is not Forge interprets none of it.
parsed = { * any => any }
